course: dictionary
lesson: 14873
title: Realism
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Realism comes from the word real. When something has realism, it looks or feels like the real thing. «The painting's realism is amazing» means the painting looks true to life, as if you could step into it.
explain: Realism can also mean seeing things as they really are and being sensible about them. «He showed a sense of realism when he saved his money for the trip» means he understood what the trip would cost and planned for it.
explain: In art and stories, realism means showing ordinary life honestly. «The writer's realism made the family feel like people we know, with arguments and jokes.» The characters feel believable because the writer shows life as it really is.
fact: Realism is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say «a sense of realism» or «with great realism», not «two realisms».
fact: «Realism» means showing people and things as they really are, in a true-to-life way.
fact: In art history, Realism was a movement in the 1800s that showed ordinary everyday life honestly.
fact: In video games, realism means graphics that look real.
fact: Realism is about how true something looks or seems, so it helps to remember the word real inside it.
exercise: «The painting's realism made the horse look ready to gallop.» What does realism mean here? | *The picture looks true to life | The picture has no colour | The picture is made of wood | The picture is very old
exercise: «Ben showed a sense of realism when he said the trip would cost more than they had.» What does a sense of realism mean? | Dreaming about things that can never happen | Being very angry about money | Doing things quickly without thinking | *Seeing things as they really are and being sensible
exercise: Which phrase from a video game review means the graphics look real? | *Amazing realism in the graphics | Cute little characters | Bright colours and loud music | Long levels and many lives
test: «The story had great realism, with families who argued and laughed like real people.» Which word is closest in meaning to realism here? | Silence | Speed | Magic | *Truth to life
test: In art history, Realism was a movement of the 1800s. What did it show? | Only animals in the wild | *Ordinary everyday life, honestly | Only the sea and the sky | Only magical castles
exam: Which sentence uses realism correctly? | The team showed realism when they planned a fair training schedule | *The painting is so full of realism that it looks like a real window | Realism ran up the hill quickly after school | I ate three realisms for lunch
